            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "text_ab_dek": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Much of what is sold as Italian leather today is made quickly and in volume, far from the hands it is named after. The workshops that still do it slowly are small, and each year there are fewer. We work with them, pay for the time a thing takes, and make in small numbers, so that what they know does not disappear.</p>",
            "width": "100%",
